<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables -.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables -.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Tuesday that Brinker International Inc, EMC Corp, Monsanto Co, Iomega Corp and 360 Communications Co were unavailable for after-hours trading for news.  </p>
<p>The exchange said Corimon SACA, Westmoreland Coal Co, Westmoreland preferred A stock and Mid-American Waste Systems were also not available.</p>
<p>360 Communications projected charges for the fourth quarter and Monsanto proposed to buy remaining shares of Calgene Inc.</p>
<p>The other three companies released their quarterly earnings.</p>
